      },
      "description": [
        "Microsoft is releasing this security advisory to provide information about a vulnerability in .NET 8.0, .NET 9.0, and .NET 10.0. This advisory also provides guidance on what developers can do to update their applications to remove this vulnerability. Heap-based buffer overflow in .NET allows an unauthorized attacker to elevate privileges locally. ",
        "WPF TrueType subsetter (DirectWriteForwarder / TtfDelta ModSbit) heap corruption via malformed EBDT table length."
